NAME
       ladder-vault - the Linux Ladder's vault (Cyber Range)

SYNOPSIS
       ladder-vault
       ladder-vault --open --step N

DESCRIPTION
       ladder-vault keeps the password for the next step of Cyber Range's Linux
       Ladder. Run with no options it only says that it is locked.

       It opens for the person who is on step N when they tell it which step
       they are on, and then prints the password for step N+1.

       ladder-vault is part of Cyber Range's pretend practice computer. It is
       not a real Linux program.

OPTIONS
       --open
              Ask the vault to open.

       --step N
              The step you are on (your user name is stepN). It must come
              after --open.

EXIT STATUS
       0 when the vault opened, 1 when it stayed locked.

EXAMPLES
       On step 17 (signed in as step17):
           ladder-vault --open --step 17

SEE ALSO
       man(1), whoami(1)
